This source code is published so that anyone can read it, audit it, and check
that the extension does what it claims. That is the point: the product exists
because a signed build was found to contain a browsing-history collector nobody
could see. Code you cannot read is a promise you cannot check.

Reading it is not the same as being free to ship it, and this licence says so
plainly.

