1. View, read, audit and study this source code, for any purpose.
2. Copy it and modify it locally, and build and run your own modified copy on
   machines you control, for your own use, evaluation, testing or security
   research.
3. Quote excerpts of it when discussing, reviewing or reporting on it, including
   in security advisories and bug reports.

